MODELS THIS STACK DEPLOYS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Llama3-OpenBioLLM-70B (aaditya/Llama3-OpenBioLLM-70B)
    The reviewer model. Weights are downloaded from Hugging Face at runtime and
    are not distributed with this repository. It is a derivative of Meta's
    Llama 3 and is governed by the META LLAMA 3 COMMUNITY LICENSE AGREEMENT,
    which is not an OSI-approved open-source licence. Among other terms it
    carries an acceptable-use policy, a condition on services exceeding 700
    million monthly active users, and a requirement to display

        "Built with Meta Llama 3"

    Review the model card and the Meta Llama 3 licence before deploying it.

gpt-oss-120b (openai/gpt-oss-120b)
    The reasoning model, served by the optional "local-gptoss" profile or by an
    endpoint you provide. Released by OpenAI under the Apache License 2.0.
    Weights are not distributed with this repository.

OpenAI and Anthropic APIs  —  optional, disabled by default
    The baseline-comparison feature (ENABLE_BASELINE_COMPARISON, default False) sends
    the same input to the OpenAI and Anthropic APIs for side-by-side comparison. It is
    off unless you enable it and supply API keys, and it is subject to those providers'
    terms rather than this licence.

vLLM (vllm/vllm-openai container image)
    Serves both models. vLLM is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. The
    published image additionally bundles NVIDIA CUDA components under NVIDIA's
    own licence terms.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA SOURCES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CollecTRI / OmniPath  —  fetched by you, not shipped
    The TF-target regulon used for upstream-regulator inference is NOT included
    in this repository. interpretation-api/src/pipeline/data/README.md explains
    how to obtain it. OmniPath aggregates resources under heterogeneous terms,
    some restricted to academic use; review them for your use case. The pipeline
    runs without this file and falls back to LLM-proposed candidates.
        Muller-Dott et al., Nucleic Acids Research, 2023 (CollecTRI)
        Turei et al., Molecular Systems Biology, 2021 (OmniPath)

KEGG  —  queried at runtime (https://rest.kegg.jp)
    Used for pathway structure (KGML) retrieval. KEGG is free for academic use
    via its website, but programmatic, bulk, or commercial access requires a
    licence from Pathway Solutions. If you deploy this commercially, resolve
    KEGG licensing first.
        Kanehisa & Goto, Nucleic Acids Research, 2000

STRING  —  queried at runtime (https://string-db.org)
    Protein-protein interaction networks for hub-gene analysis. Distributed
    under CC BY 4.0, which requires attribution.
        Szklarczyk et al., Nucleic Acids Research

Reactome  —  queried at runtime (https://reactome.org)
    Pathway structure. Released under CC0.
        Milacic et al., Nucleic Acids Research

Pathway Commons  —  queried at runtime (https://www.pathwaycommons.org)
    Interaction evidence. Aggregates sources with per-source terms.
        Rodchenkov et al., Nucleic Acids Research


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ALGORITHMS REIMPLEMENTED (no third-party code copied)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Markov Clustering
    Step 1 groups pathways into themes using MCL.
        van Dongen, "Graph Clustering by Flow Simulation", PhD thesis,
        University of Utrecht, 2000
    Implemented via the markov_clustering package (MIT).

aPEAR default parameters
    The clustering parameters in
    interpretation-api/src/pipeline/services/pathway_clustering_service.py
    mirror the published defaults of aPEAR (ievaKer/aPEAR). The parameter
    choices were read from that project's documentation; no code was copied.
        Kersevicius & Gordevicius, Bioinformatics, 2023


